@* Writing, in four steps: the second motion tutorial, built the same way as
   HowToCall. The third step is the one that matters: the words are yours. *@

<figure class="act-tut" aria-labelledby="tut-write-title">
    <figcaption id="tut-write-title" class="act-tut-title">A message, in four steps <span>about ten minutes</span></figcaption>
    <ol class="act-tut-steps">
        <li class="act-tut-step" style="--i: 0">
            <svg class="act-tut-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M10 12h44v28H30L20 50V40H10z" />
                <path class="act-draw" pathLength="1" d="M18 26h24" />
            </svg>
            <strong>Say why, in a sentence</strong>
            <span>A worry, a job, a kid, a neighbourhood. Why it matters to you is what a staffer remembers.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="act-tut-step" style="--i: 1">
            <svg class="act-tut-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true">
                <rect x="14" y="8" width="36" height="48" rx="3" />
                <path class="act-draw" pathLength="1" d="M22 18h20M22 26h20M22 34h20M22 42h20M22 50h10" />
            </svg>
            <strong>Get a first draft</strong>
            <span>Your reason, the facts, and one clear ask, laid out the way offices read them.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="act-tut-step" style="--i: 2">
            <svg class="act-tut-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true">
                <g class="act-scribble"><path d="M14 50l4-12 26-26 8 8-26 26z" /><path d="M40 16l8 8" /></g>
            </svg>
            <strong>Make it yours</strong>
            <span>Change anything. A message in your own voice counts for more than a perfect one.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="act-tut-step" style="--i: 3">
            <svg class="act-tut-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true">
                <g class="act-fly"><rect x="8" y="18" width="44" height="30" rx="2" /><path d="M8 20l22 16 22-16" /></g>
            </svg>
            <strong>Send it yourself</strong>
            <span>From your own email or the office&rsquo;s form. It comes from you, not from us.</span>
        </li>
    </ol>
</figure>
